## Forbidden behaviors

| ❌ NEVER | ✅ INSTEAD |
|---|---|
| Hard-code geography, craft, niche, or supplier network | Capture in profile each session — ZERO assumed access |
| Reuse a prior session's example topic as scaffolding | Start every run fresh from user's actual input |
| Use regex to "extract" revenue | Read claims with semantic LLM understanding, tag confidence |
| Fabricate revenue numbers from anecdotes | Cite real sources or say "no evidence" |
| Cluster by tier-bucket | Reason about each opportunity individually with 5-property test |
| Surface cluster of n=2 as "trend" | Require ≥3 real verified references per opportunity |
| Ignore counterfactual saturation | Always run anti-confirmation queries |
| Use `pipeline_drop_on_fail`, `archetype-allocator`, etc. | None of those exist in nui-hunter — that was V20 theater |
| Output P90/P50 as if rigorous | If you don't have audited financials, give RANGES with confidence intervals + provenance |
| Output 5-property scores (X/50) | Use Q1/Q2/ratio/compounding binary test |
| Mark MOUNTAIN without `pulse_replies` | Use MOUNTAIN_CANDIDATE → pause for Step 6.5 pulse |
| Cap downside at zero | Always estimate real downside loss (time, capital, opportunity) |
| Skip Step 6.5 silently | Print blocking message + exit cleanly |

## Acceptance test (does this command work?)

Run `/stage0 "<arbitrary topic from user>"` with any profile. The rubric is topic-agnostic — it MUST produce these structural properties regardless of domain:

- Step 6 outputs a deterministic verdict from Q1 / Q2 / ratio / compounding — NOT a weighted sum.
- If Q1 cannot be proven with a real founder URL at ≥$10K/mo net → verdict ∈ {INSUFFICIENT_SIGNAL, KILL, SIDE_HUSTLE}.
- Verdict **MUST NOT** be `MOUNTAIN` or `PROVISIONAL_MOUNTAIN` without a populated `pulse_replies` array with ≥1 `buying_now` / `researching` reply.
- Any "PURSUE X/50" style sum-score output is a test failure.
- Verdict saved to `verdicts/`. Case persisted to `kb/cases/` only if verdict ∈ {MOUNTAIN, PROVISIONAL_MOUNTAIN, SIDE_HUSTLE, KILL}.

Intentionally no fixed example topic — examples bias the LLM toward the last-seen niche. Topics must be discovered each run.

